<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo#"
     xml:base="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:obo="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:rheo="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:oboInOwl="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/0.4.0/rheo.owl"/>
        <dcterms:bibliographicCitation>Baines D, Ashley M. Real Health Economics Ontology (RHEO), version 0.3.0. Intelligent Parameters Ltd; 2026. https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/0.4.0/rheo.owl. Licence CC BY 4.0.</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
        <dcterms:created>2026-10-07</dcterms:created>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678"/>
        <dcterms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731"/>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">An ontology of health economic reality and of the evidence built from it. It describes the persons, organizations, households, resources and care settings involved in health care; what happens to and between them (care processes, resource use, patient movements, payments, behaviours, clinical events and changes of state); the records that describe these things (state observations and transitions, classification revisions, resource use, costs under a perspective, tariffs, payments, stocks and flows); and the population specifications, estimands, estimates, uncertainty, assumptions, sources, model parameters, parameter assignments, model versions and results built from them. It allows a model result to be traced to the estimates and assumptions it used and to the documents those estimates came from. RHEO is aligned to BFO 2020 (ISO/IEC 21838-2) and reuses IAO, OBI, COB, STATO, OGMS, OMRSE, RO and PROV-O terms. Its links to the Health Economics Ontology (HEO) are published as an SSSOM mapping file. Policy: HEO identifies concepts and organises their meanings with SKOS; RHEO defines types, each classified within BFO, with its own IRI, name, definition and relationships. A HEO concept and a RHEO type have different identities even when their names are alike, and a RHEO type never uses a HEO concept URI as its identifier. The RNI typology of changes of state is kept in a separate module (the reading adopted for 0.3.0) (rheo-rni.ttl), and the dependence between uncertain quantities in an extension module (rheo-uncertainty.ttl); the core does not depend on either.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:issued>2026-10-16</dcterms:issued>
        <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <dcterms:modified>2026-10-16</dcterms:modified>
        <dcterms:publisher>Intelligent Parameters Ltd</dcterms:publisher>
        <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Real Health Economics Ontology (RHEO)</dcterms:title>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>rheo</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/rheo/RHEO_</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Pre-1.0 release (status alpha) for review by its creators and invited reviewers; terms, definitions and mappings may still change before version 1.0. BFO 2020 is imported; the BFO terms RHEO uses are also declared here with their BFO 2020 labels and definitions. Other external terms from IAO, OBI and COB, STATO, OGMS, OMRSE, VO, NCBI Taxonomy, RO and PROV-O are referenced by their original identifiers with label, official definition and asserted parent; consult the source ontologies for their full axioms.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heo"/>
        <owl:versionInfo>0.4.0 (alpha)</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


